 # Hierarchical Volume Traversal with Adaptive Termination
 
-Also called: Pyramidal Volume Traversal, TraceRay2
+Also called: Combined Hierarchical Enumeration and Adaptive Termination, Levoy's Ray Tracing Optimizations, Pyramidal Volume Traversal, TraceRay2
 
 ## Overview
-Hierarchical Volume Traversal with Adaptive Termination is a ray tracing algorithm that uses a pyramidal data structure of binary volumes to skip empty regions and an adaptive termination criterion to stop tracing when opacity changes become negligible [S1]. Unlike geometric ray tracing, which uses bounding volumes or spatial subdivision with lists of primitives, this method uses a hierarchical binary volume structure, which is more efficient for volume data because volume datasets have tens of millions of spatially ordered cells with single samples, whereas geometric scenes have hundreds of cells with many primitives [S1].
+Hierarchical Volume Traversal with Adaptive Termination is a ray tracing algorithm that uses a pyramidal data structure of binary volumes to skip empty regions and an adaptive termination criterion to stop tracing when accumulated opacity exceeds a threshold [S1]. Unlike geometric ray tracing, which uses bounding volumes or spatial subdivision with lists of primitives, this method uses a hierarchical binary volume structure, which is more efficient for volume data because volume datasets have tens of millions of spatially ordered cells with single samples, whereas geometric scenes have hundreds of cells with many primitives [S1].
 
